    "name": "Intercity Seoul Hotel",
    "detail": "I've been in Seoul twice before this trip and can say that it was my worst travel. Hotel rooms are small for the price they want. We didn't get toothbrushes and toothpaste, shampoo was cheap-quality, shower had no door. We didn't get even cups for coffee, just plastic glasses. Slippers are reusable. On the first day I heard some noise from workers. It seemed like they drilled walls somewhere nearby the floor at about 10pm. Air conditioner worked only for hot mode. If you are too hot, you need to open windows with all the city noise. Floors are cold and we didn't find any controller for warming them up. Supposedly they don't have such function. In a nutshell, if I chose the hotel, I would find better one and cheaper. Not recommend at all.",
